# Core Workflow

- **Cursor** = IDE harness; **Claude Code CLI** = terminal harness.
- Use highest-tier model variants (Opus/Sonnet thinking, GPT extra-high) for planning and review.
- Start **new sessions** instead of compacting long context.
- Keep PRs **minimal** — one concern per PR when possible.
- Plan before build; read Graphify reports for reference-modeled features.
- After each feature: code-structure pass → security-review → Greptile/CodeRabbit loop.

## Commands

```bash
node scripts/sync-sources.mjs
node scripts/index-reference.mjs <name>
node scripts/new-project.mjs <name> [template]
```

## Do not

- Broad refactors in feature PRs.
- Install packages newer than 7 days without explicit approval.
- Add high-risk MCPs (filesystem, postgres, memory) by default.
